{"slug":"BV.148.5","title":"Svara Saṅghāta: Note Combinations","printed_no":"19","sloka_from":null,"sloka_to":null,"summary":"Mostly tables: four-beat note clusters (svarasaṃghāta) in Bhūpālī, from two and three notes, then grouped by first and last note (Ga to Sa, Pa to Pa, Sāṃ to Ga and others). Words guide the tongue, ṭa falling only on syllables; it ends with practice for a rāga with śuddha Ni up and komal Ni down.","khanda":{"slug":"pradarshana","title":"Part Three: Performance"},"prev":{"slug":"BV.147.2","title":"Rāga Bhūpālī: Ascent and Descent"},"next":{"slug":"BV.148.27","title":"An Introduction to Rāga Khamāj"},"blocks":[{"id":"BV.148.5","kind":"heading","n":null,"level":4,"text":"Svarasaṅghāta (clusters of notes)"},{"id":"BV.148.6","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>With two notes</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>Re</td><td>Re</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>Re</td><td>Re</td><td>Sa</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>Re</td><td>Sa</td><td>Re</td><td>Sa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.7","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>With three notes</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>Re</td><td>Ga</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>Ga</td><td>Re</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>Re</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaGa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>SaRe</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaGa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>ReRe</td><td>Ga</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.8","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>With more than three notes (from Ga to Sa)</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Ga</td><td>Ga</td><td>Re</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>GaRe</td><td>-Ga</td><td>ReGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPa</td><td>GaPaDhaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPa</td><td>GaReGa-</td><td>PaGa-Re</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>Ga</td><td>-Pa</td><td>DhaPa-Ga</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPaDhaPa</td><td>GaPa</td><td>GaReGaRe</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPaDhaPa</td><td>DhaṠaDhaPa</td><td>GaReSaRe</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>GaReReRe</td><td>PaGaGaGa</td><td>DhaPaPaPa</td><td>GaReSa-</td></tr><tr><td>GaPaGaPa</td><td>DhaPaDhaPa</td><td>ṠaDhaṠaDha</td><td>PaGaReSa</td></tr><tr><td>Ga-Pa</td><td>-DhaPa-</td><td>Ga-ReSa</td><td>-ReSa-</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.9","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Ṡa to Sa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>ṠaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>Sa-</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaDha</td><td>ṠaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>Ṡa-</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>-Ga</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaṘe</td><td>ṠaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaDhaPa</td><td>GaDhaPa</td><td>PaGaRe</td><td>GaReSa</td></tr><tr><td>SaReGaRe</td><td>ṠaṘeṠaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.10","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Pa to Sa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Pa</td><td>Ga</td><td>Re</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ṘeSa</td></tr><tr><td>PaGaReGa</td><td>Pa</td><td>GaPaGaRe</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDha</td><td>-Pa</td><td>-Ga</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDha</td><td>PaDhaPaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>ReGaReSa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDha</td><td>ṠaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td><td>Ḋha</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDhaṠa-</td><td>DhaṠa-Dha</td><td>PaDha-Dha</td><td>GaRe-Sa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDhaṠaṘe</td><td>ĠaReṠaṘe</td><td>ṠaDhaPaGa</td><td>ReGaReSa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDhaṠaPa</td><td>DhaṠaPaDha</td><td>ṠaṘeṠaDha</td><td>PaGaReSa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.11","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Dha to Sa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Dha</td><td>Pa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td>Dha</td><td>PaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDhaDhaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>PaPaPaPa</td><td>GaReSa-</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaDha</td><td>PaDha</td><td>ReSa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaṠaDha</td><td>PaDhaPa</td><td>GaPaGa</td><td>ReSa-</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>GaPaDhaṠa</td><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>GaReSa-</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>SaReSaSa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaṠaṘeĠa</td><td>ṘeṠaDhaPa</td><td>GaPaPaDha</td><td>PaGaReSa</td></tr><tr><td>Dha-DhaDha</td><td>-DhaPaGa</td><td>Pa-PaGa</td><td>-ReSa-</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.12","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Sa to Pa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>SaRe</td><td>SaRe</td><td>Ga-ReGa</td><td>ReGaPa-</td></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>Re</td><td>Ga</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>SaRe</td><td>GaPa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>Sa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>-Dha</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>SaRe</td><td>-Ga</td><td>-Dha</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>SaDha</td><td>Sa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>PaPa</td></tr><tr><td>SaRe</td><td>SaDha</td><td>SaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>SaDha</td><td>SaRe</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>SaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>RePa</td><td>GaPa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.13","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Ga to Pa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>GaPa</td><td>Dha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>Ga</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>GaRe</td><td>GaRe</td><td>SaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>PaGa</td><td>PaDha</td><td>ReSa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>GaMa</td><td>RePa</td><td>PaGa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>GaRe</td><td>SaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>Ga</td><td>-</td><td>Pa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPaDha</td><td>PaDhaṠa</td><td>DhaPaGa</td><td>ReGaPa</td></tr><tr><td>GaPaGa-</td><td>Re-GaRe</td><td>SaReGa-</td><td>ReGaPa-</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.14","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Pa to Pa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Pa</td><td>Ga</td><td>Dha</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>PaGa</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>-Pa</td></tr><tr><td>PaGa</td><td>ReSa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDha</td><td>PaṠa</td><td>DhaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDha</td><td>ṠaPa</td><td>DhaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>PaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>SaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDhaṠa-</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaPaDhaPa</td><td>-Pa</td></tr><tr><td>PaDhaPaGa</td><td>-ReSaRe</td><td>Ga--Dha</td><td>Pa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.15","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Dha to Pa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>DhaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaDha</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaGa</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaDha</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>PaGa</td><td>PaPa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>Sa-ReGa</td><td>PaDha</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPa</td><td>DhaGa</td><td>PaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPaGa</td><td>PaGaRe</td><td>SaReGa</td><td>ReGaPa</td></tr><tr><td>Dha-</td><td>PaGa</td><td>-Re</td><td>GaPa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.16","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Ṡa to Pa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>ṠaṘe</td><td>ṘeṠa</td><td>ṠaDha</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaGa</td><td>ṘeṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaDha</td><td>ṠaPa</td><td>DhaGa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaṠaṘe</td><td>DhaDhaṠa</td><td>PaPaDha</td><td>GaGaPa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaDha</td><td>-Pa</td><td>-Ga</td><td>Pa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.17","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Re to Pa</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Re</td><td>Ga</td><td>Dha</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>ReGa</td><td>ReSa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>Pa</td></tr><tr><td>ReGa</td><td>PaDha</td><td>Sa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr><tr><td>ReSa</td><td>DhaSa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaPa</td></tr><tr><td>ReGa</td><td>PaDha</td><td>ṠaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.18","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Ṡa to Ga</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>ṠaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaPa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaPa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaDha</td><td>-Pa</td><td>-Ga</td><td>ReGa</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaṠa</td><td>ṘeṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaĠa</td><td>ṘeĠaṘeṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaṘeĠa-</td><td>ṘeĠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>ṠaṘeĠa</td><td>ṘeṠaṘe</td><td>ṠaDhaṠa</td><td>DhaPaGa</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.19","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Dha to Ga</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>Dha</td><td>Dha</td><td>Pa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>Dha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>Re</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPa</td><td>-DhaGa</td><td>Re</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>DhaDha</td><td>PaDha</td><td>-Pa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>DhaṠa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>ṠaDha</td><td>PaGa</td></tr><tr><td>DhaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>Dha-Ṡa</td><td>Dha-Pa</td><td>Dha-Pa</td><td>Ga--</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>SaRe</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>Sa-ReGa</td><td>Pa-ReGa</td><td>Ga</td></tr><tr><td>DhaṠa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>GaPa</td><td>Ga</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.20","kind":"table","n":null,"table_html":"<table class=\"bv-table\"><caption>From Ga to Dha</caption><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td>GaRe</td><td>Sa</td><td>ReGa</td><td>PaDha</td></tr><tr><td>GaRe</td><td>SaRe</td><td>GaPa</td><td>Dha</td></tr><tr><td>GaDha</td><td>PaDha</td><td>PaGa</td><td>PaDha</td></tr><tr><td>GaRe</td><td>PaGa</td><td>DhaPa</td><td>ṠaDha</td></tr><tr><td>GaGa</td><td>GaRe</td><td>GaGa</td><td>ṠaDha</td></tr><tr><td>0Ga</td><td>-Re</td><td>Ga</td><td>PaDha</td></tr><tr><td>-Ga</td><td>-Re</td><td>Ga</td><td>PaDha</td></tr><tr><td>0Ga</td><td>-Re</td><td>GaPaDhaṠa</td><td>Dha</td></tr><tr><td>GaPa</td><td>DhaPaGaRe</td><td>GaPa</td><td>Dha</td></tr><tr><td>Ga-PaDha</td><td>Pa-GaRe</td><td>GaGaPaDha</td><td>Dha</td></tr><tr><td>GaGa</td><td>RePa</td><td>PaGa</td><td>PaDha</td></tr><tr><td>GaPa</td><td>-Dha</td><td>-Sa</td><td>Dha</td></tr><tr><td>GaRe</td><td>GaPa</td><td>Dha</td><td>-</td></tr></table>","caption":""},{"id":"BV.148.21","kind":"prose","n":null,"text":"Bigger groups of notes can also be made by joining the small groups given above to one another. These can be used in any gat or song on the basis of the tāla. So that composing tāns (fast runs) bound to tāla, and practising them, becomes still easier, the help of words will be necessary for this ease. Then, notes bound in words are not forgotten. From those words we will also get the hint that the tongue (jībh, zubān) is to be used with the syllables: where one long syllable stands on several notes, the tongue will be used there on only one note, and the remaining notes will be expressed only by placing and lifting the finger. For example, if we play this group (PaDha Ṡa Dha Pa) without the help of words, then out of habit the tongue will be used on all the notes, like (ṭaṭa ṭā ṭā ṭā); and if it gets the support of words, the tongue will have to be used only on the letters standing in the words - PaDha Ṡa Dha Pa, mā- - dhapa pa, ṭā- - ṭā ṭā"},{"id":"BV.148.22","kind":"prose","n":null,"text":"The point is that for a note above or below which a syllable is written, the use of (ṭā) is proper; and a note below or above which the khaṇḍākāra mark (-) is written instead of a syllable should be made clear with the finger alone, without (ṭa). In the early period it is hard to carry out this action. To make this difficulty easy, one should practise for a long time in the form of alaṅkāras (patterned exercises), using many notes on one (ṭa) and many (ṭa) on one note. For example -"},{"id":"BV.148.23","kind":"prose","n":null,"text":"Many notes on one ṭa - Sa Re Ga Ma ṭā - - -"},{"id":"BV.148.24","kind":"prose","n":null,"text":"Many ṭa on one note - Sa Sa Sa Sa ṭa ṭa ṭa ṭa"},{"id":"BV.148.25","kind":"prose","n":null,"text":"If there is no success in this action, no song can be imitated or followed. If the svaralipi (notation) of a song reaches us in written form, and I also have exact knowledge of the signs of the notation, then we can sing that song according to that notation. But there will be full success in playing it on the bānsurī and other suṣira vādyas (wind instruments) only when I can have correct control over the tongue as well, along with my phūṅk (breath into the bānsurī) and fingers."},{"id":"BV.148.26","kind":"prose","n":null,"text":"Groups of notes can be composed in other rāgas according to the rule given before. Then, by binding them in tāla with the help of some poem, a song or gat can be composed. Now a rāga can be mentioned for which the śāstra prescribes śuddha (natural) 'Ni' in the ascent and komal (flat) 'Ni' in the descent. To master this rāga there will be particular inconvenience with a six-hole bānsurī. To remove that inconvenience, the practitioner should make more groups of notes like the following and practise them carefully and slowly, then play those same groups quickly. If possible, practise in single and double [tempo], and keep in mind that while playing ṆiSa the whole finger will be lifted. But while playing NiDha, for komal Ni the finger is to be lowered halfway or even less than halfway. If 'Dha' is varjit (omitted) in some rāga, then also practise separately lowering one and a half fingers to play komal Ni Pa."}],"figures":[]}